{"id": "8046f21b-5d2c-454a-9db5-67a6aa7d8e9a", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "This is turning out to be more involved than a simple SG/NACL lookup — the source IP (10.0.1.5) sits in a VPC named "Overlap" connected via Transit Gateway, and 10.0.2.9 isn't in any subnet of that VPC. Let me dig into the Transit Gateway routing and NACLs/security groups to find the actual blocking rule.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_SrwowSSvgRZVJWwOJtrYTI", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"prompt": "{
  "task": "Determine which rule (security group, network ACL, or Transit Gateway route table) caused a REJECT of TCP traffic from 10.0.1.5:51000 to 10.0.2.9:3389 (RDP), with no reverse-direction flow log entry at all.",
